<s-1 id="RM000000FSU00TX_01_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___000047700000">
<ptxt>Road Test</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<atten2>
<ptxt>Make sure that the road is safe before performing the test.</ptxt>
</atten2>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Be sure to perform this after inspecting and adjusting the engine.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Perform the test at normal operating CVT fluid temperature (50 to 100°C).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Perform the test with the A/C OFF.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>Road Test List</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.32in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="4.76in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection and Check Procedure</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>D Position Shift Function</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Check that the transmission shifts during normal driving (typical city driving). (Inspect based on the shift schedule)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Transmission Control Switch Operation </ptxt>
<ptxt>(D ←→ M Selector Switch Operation)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Move the shift lever to the M position and check that gears can be changed with sequential shifting.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Kick-down Function</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Check that kick-down occurs according to the shift schedule.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine Braking</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 7 gear in the M position (approximately 90 to 100km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 6 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 6 gear in the M position (approximately 70 to 80km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 5 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 5 gear in the M position (approximately 50 to 60km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 4 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 4 gear in the M position (approximately 40 to 50km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 3 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 3 gear in the M position (approximately 30 to 40km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 2 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in 2 gear in the M position (approximately 20 to 30km/h), shift to "-" on the sequential gate and check engine braking in 1 gear.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P Position Operation</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Stop the vehicle on a slope (approximately 5° or more), apply the parking brake in the P position, and check that the vehicle does not move when the parking brake is released.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Abnormal Noise, Vibration</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Check for abnormal noise and vibration while driving and during shifting.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</atten4>
</content1>
